  <data name="HelpTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Usage</value></data>
  <data name="HelpContent" xml:space="preserve"><value>MobilePackageGen GUI - Package Extractor

Steps:
1. Click "Open Image..." to select a disk image (FFU/VHDX/WIM/IMG/BIN)
2. Wait for the program to enumerate all extractable packages
3. Check the packages you want to extract in the tree (grouped by type and partition)
4. Use the filter to filter by type, or search in the search box
5. Click "Select All"/"Deselect All" for quick selection
6. Set the output folder at the bottom
7. Click "Build Selected" to start extraction

Package Types:
- CBS: Windows Component Packages (.mum manifests)
- SPKG: Mobile Component Packages (.xml manifests)
- Driver: Driver Packages (.inf drivers)

Notes:
- A console window opens at startup showing build logs and progress
- Packages with errors are skipped automatically and summarized at the end
- Output folder contains subfolders named by partition</value></data>
